From 68ae9b93ae9f2f5eb37711c1aa161fda315a0144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:48:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: unsaved-changes pill, DNS Director device picker,
 Dreadwatch names itself, form fixes (102.8 line)

- www/reaper/reaper_pending.js (new): "Unsaved changes: N" + Discard, the kit pages' cue, for the
  pages that keep list edits on the page until their Apply / Save - QoS, Policy Routing, WAN Ports,
  Wallguard, Dreadwatch. Owner on metal: a QoS rule's x edited only the page and nothing said Apply
  was owed, so the delete was never written. Each page passes a snapshot of what its Apply / Save
  writes; Wallguard's Save builds its request in shPayload() (byte-identical requests).
- DNS Director (Reaper_DNS.asp): a picker of connected devices before the MAC box (the stock page
  had a client list); offline devices and devices that already have a rule are left out; typing a
  MAC still works.
- Dreadwatch: the apply overlay and the how-it-works card used Warden's strings; RDWT_66 / RDWT_67
  in all 25 packs (each pack derived from its own Wallguard / Warden text).
- VPN Director: one card per client, tags on their own line. Wireless Settings: the band dot is the
  radio's state, as on the dashboard (it was a per-radio colour). Wallguard / Dreadwatch "Add a
  source": Request and the key header fold away for a plain list; the API key field is styled.
- EN.dict VLAN_port_binding_note: "In use by %@." (was "This port(s) is using by %@.").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
